{"base_rate":0.2742155525238745,"brier":0.13423833560709414,"bss":0.3255079760969587,"bss_hi":0.4344076719203652,"bss_lo":0.17145627829574922,"chart":{"base":[417.6,59.5],"fp":[182.3,256.5],"lead":"62,254.2 272,220.8 482,192.7 692,135.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.33 — higher than 60% of cities","fp":"low end -2pp, high end +26pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 53% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 100% → rained 83%"},"rel":"64.1,463 212.7,429.3 559.1,282.5 690.2,106.5"},"country":"CN","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1397407912687585,"ess":330.5833440599769,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Shanghai</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Shanghai rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 733 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 19.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.33, ranked 85 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(42&ndash;157) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>285</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>149</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Shanghai</b> <span class=\"muted\">China</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.33</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>42&ndash;157\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>733 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Shanghai &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Shanghai\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.18,378.1684210526316 97.07111111111111,314.5925925925926 193.94583333333335,200.0 300.2933333333333,98.88888888888886 373.39486486486487,32.75675675675677 411.0021476510067,18.0 411.0021476510067,22.885906040268424 373.39486486486487,86.86486486486484 300.2933333333333,169.66666666666666 193.94583333333335,280.8888888888889 97.07111111111111,364.0246913580247 59.18,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"282.1855388813097\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"282.1855388813097\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.18,379.4456140350877 97.07111111111111,373.01234567901236 193.94583333333335,326.3888888888889 300.2933333333333,235.38888888888889 373.39486486486487,219.67567567567568 411.0021476510067,79.07382550335569\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 285 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"59.18\" cy=\"379.4456140350877\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"97.07111111111111\" cy=\"373.01234567901236\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 38%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"193.94583333333335\" cy=\"326.3888888888889\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 68%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"300.2933333333333\" cy=\"235.38888888888889\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 89%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"373.39486486486487\" cy=\"219.67567567567568\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 149 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.0021476510067\" cy=\"79.07382550335569\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(27%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Shanghai the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.56) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.21).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.206</td><td class='num'>16.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.251</td><td class='num'>20.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>211</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.317</td><td class='num'>13.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>0.561</td><td class='num'>4.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":31.22222,"lon":121.45806,"n":733,"n_cities":213,"name":"Shanghai","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0033333333333333335,"n":285,"obs":0.007017543859649123,"sig":false},{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.11037037037037037,"n":81,"obs":0.024691358024691357,"sig":true},{"hi":0.57,"l